greetings Nephilim and welcome to patch  210 my name is Brandi camel also known  as novelist asst community  representative for Diablo 3 and your  host for today in this video we'll be  reviewing our first major content patch  for Reaper of souls let's get started  our biggest feature is a competitive  system we're calling seasons seasons are  similar to diablo two ladders and offer  heroes the opportunity to play fresh new  characters from level one seasons are  considered a completely separate game  mode as a result seasonal characters  will have their own stash artisan  progression gold and Paragon levels you  can create both normal and hardcore  seasonal characters let's talk about  seasonal rewards many new legendaries  will be introduced with each season and  seasonal characters will have the first  opportunity to get their hands on these  items if seasons aren't your thing don't  worry once the season ends these items  will be added to the regular loop pool  so everyone will have a chance to find  them each season participants will also  earn one piece from a new and exclusive  transmogrification set every season you  play will net you a new piece from this  special set so join the fun and you'll  get to show off in style conquests our  new season only achievements they  represent a variety of challenges from  defeating malthael on torment 6 to speed  running the entire campaign in under an  hour conquests are available to both  normal and hardcore heroes so you'll be  able to tackle these challenges in your  preferred game mode conquests grant  achievement points that contribute  toward your seasonal total they're also  tracked on the regional leader boards on  a first-come first-served basis the  first 1000 players to complete a  conquest will be immortalized on the  leaderboards for that season when a  season ends your seasonal characters  will become standard hardcore or normal  mode heroes as appropriate rewards  you've earned during a season including  items Gold artisan recipes Paragon  experience and achievements will all  carry over any items left in your  seasonal stash will be mailed to  in addition two seasons were also  introducing greater risks greater rifts  are a competitive form of Nephilim rifts  featuring a progress timer you'll have  15 minutes to spawn and defeat the rift  guardian and faster runs will bring  greater rewards to enter a greater rift  you'll first need to acquire a keystone  of trials from a regular rift guardian  and then visit the Nephilim obelisk in  town to enter the realm of trials the  realm of trials is a small arena  designed to evaluate your ability to  defeat waves of enemies upon completing  this trial you'll receive an  appropriately challenging greater rift  key to create a greater rift portal  simply bring your greater rift key to  the Nephilim obelisk in town strong  enough to survive the trials greater  rifts are tracked by a new progress bar  that compares your monster kill count to  the time remaining monsters grant  progress based on their health and level  of difficulty so tackling those elite  and champion packs will have a greater  payoff than your average minion note  that monsters in greater risk don't drop  loop and the rewards for the entire  greater rift will instead drop off the  rift guardian at the end greater risks  are much more challenging and should be  played strategically when playing in  greater rifts please keep the following  rules in mind some resurrection and  teleport functions have been disabled in  addition you will be unable to swap gear  or skills while in a greater rift so be  sure to plan accordingly when you defeat  a greater rift guardian you'll be  visited by a new NPC named oshi if you  complete your greater rift before time  expires you'll have two options for  rewards a chance to add a rank to one of  your existing legendary gems or a higher  level greater rift keystone should your  time expire in a greater rift the rift  Guardian will automatically be summoned  while you won't be able to continue your  greater rift journey after the Guardian  has been defeated you'll still have the  chance to upgrade one of your legendary  gems potentially adding multiple ranks  at higher greater rift levels aim high  and you'll be greatly rewarded for your  efforts  to support seasons and greater rifts  we're adding leaderboards for each  system these leaderboards will allow  players to track their progress for  greater rifts seasonal achievement  points and seasonal conquests designed  to be informative in detailed  leaderboards will allow you to compare  your progress to that of your gameplay  region friends and clan members and each  type of board will track progress a  little differently greater rift  leaderboards will display rankings for  both hardcore and normal heroes as well  as seasonal and non-seasonal heroes in  addition you'll be able to sort them by  group composition including solo play  for each class 2 player 3 player and 4  player groups as conquests and seasonal  achievement point totals our season only  features these leaderboards will only  track information for seasonal  characters conquests and achievement  points are account-wide so while some  challenges may require playing in a  particular mode there's no need to sort  normal and hard core information  separately  while many items are being revisited in  patch 210 we want to highlight some  specific overhauls first off two-handed  weapons have received an increase in  base damage across the board this damage  will apply retroactively Lee and any  two-handed weapons you already have will  be automatically updated we've also  added unique powers to several existing  legendary items existing versions of  these legendaries will not be  retrofitted with these new abilities so  you shouldn't feel the need to hang on  to them  have you ever wondered what's on the  other side of that treasure goblins  portal wonder no more with patch 210  each time you defeat a treasure goblin  there's a small chance to leave behind a  portal to the vault this mystical area  features dangerous new enemies and  riches beyond your wildest dreams so  don't let that next Goblin get away  we've also added a new environment to  Nephilim rifts the cesspools the  cesspools were originally designed as  the sewers of Westmarch while we  couldn't fit them into act 5 for the  release of Reaper of souls you now have  a chance to explore this festering dank  environment in any greater or regular  Nephilim rift this wraps up our overview  of patch 210 while we've covered some of  the largest features there's plenty more  to discover in our patch notes so be  sure to check them out we also encourage  you to share your thoughts about this  update on the Diablo 3 forums and we  hope you'll join us as we gear up for  our very first season thanks for  watching and we'll see you in sanctuary
 

